  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What the shape buys a builder",
      "items": [
        "Per stage meters at the gateway are where a cost estimate comes from, before the build rather than after it",
        "A trace per step is what answers \"Why did it do that?\" without reading a log",
        "A checkpoint commit per step, so a bad step is one revert rather than a rebuild"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Boundaries that do real work",
      "items": [
        "Secrets reach the sandbox at run time and never enter model context",
        "One sandbox per build with an egress allowlist, so a generated command cannot reach the platform",
        "Deployed apps hold no provider keys: they call agents through the runtime proxy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Proposed, not built",
      "items": [
        "This is the target architecture, written up in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md",
        "The demo implements sign in, per user Postgres rows and live decision model calls",
        "What runs today is the separate system architecture diagram"
      ]
    }
  ]
